    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0230" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.003 Wallace, Henry A./39</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stettinius</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-03-08">March 8, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: The Vice President asked me to
                    call on him yesterday. He stated the President had asked him to take a trip,
                    later this spring, to Chungking. Mr. Wallace wanted to visit India as well as
                    Moscow.</p>
                <p>The Vice President asked me if I would discuss the matter with the President
                    today, which I have done. The President has definitely told me that he doesn’t
                    want the Vice President to go to India, Moscow, or to the fighting areas in the
                    Pacific, but he was agreeable to the Vice President’s visiting Northern Siberia
                    to investigate industrial and agricultural matters there. I have reported this
                    to Mr. Wallace.</p>
                <p>Mr. Wallace further asked whether or not we would think it satisfactory for him
                    to invite Mr. William Herridge<anchor n="1" xml:id="d198-f1"/> as a companion on
                    the trip. I discussed this with the President, and his reaction was negative. He
                    asked, however, that I communicate with Mackenzie King.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d198-f2"/> In consultation with Mr. Dunn,<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d198-f3"/> he suggested that I make the inquiry through Ray
                    Atherton, which I have done<anchor n="4" xml:id="d198-f4"/> and I have asked Mr.
                    Atherton to send to you direct Mackenzie King’s reaction.<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d198-f5"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E[<hi rendition="#small-caps">dward</hi>] S[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >tettinius</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
